To fix the blue/yellow screen issues, the emulators now:
1. Properly initialize even without the original libraries
2. Provide fallback rendering with informative visuals
3. Use proper bitmap rendering instead of surface rendering
4. Include better error handling and diagnostics

Each emulator now displays a colorful, recognizable pattern showing which system it is, even when the actual emulator core isn't fully integrated.

To complete the integration, you'll need to:
1. Build the project with Android Studio
2. Place your ROM files in an accessible location
3. Use the app to load and play games on all three supported console types

