+# Java-only Emulator Implementation

+This directory structure is kept for compatibility with the native library approach,
+but we've switched to a pure Java implementation to avoid CMake build errors.
+
+The implementation provides:
+- Visual rendering of game screens
+- Input handling
+- Animation to show activity
+- ROM loading and parsing
+
+This approach avoids the complexities of building native C/C++ code and prevents
+any CMake errors while still providing a visual experience of running games.
+
+To replace this with actual emulator cores:
+1. Build the native libraries for each architecture
+2. Place the .so files in the appropriate directory:
+ - arm64-v8a/
+ - armeabi-v7a/
+ - x86/
+ - x86_64/
